foundation.solution_text:
Stationary points at $x = -1$ and $x = 1$ become $x$-intercepts of $f'(x)$.
$f(x)$ is increasing for $x < -1$ and $x > 1$, so $f'(x) > 0$.
$f(x)$ is decreasing for $-1 < x < 1$, so $f'(x) < 0$.
The derivative is an upward parabola with roots at $x = -1$ and $x = 1$.

