development.solution_text:
Stationary point at $x = 0 \implies f'(0) = 0$ ($x$-intercept at the origin).
For $x < 0$, $f(x)$ is increasing $\implies f'(x) > 0$.
For $x > 0$, $f(x)$ is decreasing $\implies f'(x) < 0$.
As $x \to \pm\infty$, $f'(x) \to 0$.

